<title>USA: Taiwanese firms to expand in California - governor.</title>
<headline>Taiwanese firms to expand in California - governor.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>California Governor Pete Wilson said on Thursday that six Taiwan-based high-technology companies are expanding their operations in California, creating 400 new jobs and investing $79 million in the state.</p>
<p>The companies are are UMAX Data Systems Inc, EliteGroup Computer Systems Inc, First International Computer Inc, Vanguard International Semiconductors Corp, DAVICOM Corp and MRT Technology Inc, Wilson said in a statement.</p>
<p>Wilson's office in Sacramento made the announcement. The governor is on a trade mission in Asia. He will return to California on January 31.</p>
</text>
